{
  "name": "secrets",
  "line": "encrypted values in the project",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A secret is a value that the project keeps encrypted and winch never prints."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Format"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A secret is encrypted with age for the recipients in winch.yaml. The !secret tag marks it, followed by the ciphertext in base64 on one line."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Where a secret stands"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A !secret stands only in a variable value: in the vars of an inventory, and in the defaults of winch.yaml and of recipes, at any depth of a list or a map. --set cannot give a secret."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Commands"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
          "winch secret init",
          "make an age key, add it to recipients"
        ],
        [
          "winch secret generate vars.<name>",
          "write a random password into the inventory"
        ],
        [
          "winch secret encrypt",
          "encrypt a value from stdin"
        ],
        [
          "winch secret rekey",
          "encrypt all secrets for the current recipients"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The age key"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "winch secret init makes a key at ~/.config/winch/age.key, or at the path in WINCH_AGE_KEY. It makes a key only when no key is there. With WINCH_AGE_IDENTITY_CMD, it makes no key and adds the public key of the command's key."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "winch reads the age identity from the output of the command in WINCH_AGE_IDENTITY_CMD, such as op read op://infra/winch/key. Without it, winch reads the file in WINCH_AGE_KEY, or else ~/.config/winch/age.key. winch validate needs no identity."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "A new member"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A new member runs winch secret init and sends the change for review. The new key can read the secrets after a member who can read them runs winch secret rekey."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A variable is secret when its value is a !secret, or when its default reads a secret variable. The plan, diffs, errors, logs, and JSON show (secret) in place of a secret, also a part of a value that comes from a secret. A filter replaces each secret value in all text that winch prints, also in output from the host. The filter also hides private keys, age identities, passwords in URLs, and well-known tokens."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Secrets in commands"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A secret in a command does not show in the process list of the host. A program that the command starts with the secret as an argument, such as psql -c, does show it."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Warnings and errors"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "winch warns about text in project files that looks like a private key or a token, and is not a !secret.",
        "winch warns about a file step whose content reads a secret and whose mode is missing or lets others read it.",
        "A !secret in a certbot hook is an error: certbot stores its hooks in a file that other users can read. A hook that reads a secret through match() fails the host."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "text": "# inventories/production.yaml\nhosts:\n  db1.acme.com: {}\ngroups:\n  all:\n    vars:\n      db_password: !secret YWdlLWVuY3J5cHRpb24ub3JnL3YxCi0+IFgyNTUxOSB...\n\n# winch.yaml\nname: acme\nrecipients:\n  - age1ql3z7hjy54pw3hyww5ayyfg7zqgvc7w3j2elw8zmrj2kg5sfn9aqmcac8p\nsteps:\n  - file:\n      path: /etc/app/db.env\n      content: !tpl \"DB_PASSWORD={{ .vars.db_password }}\\n\"\n      mode: \"0600\"\n"
    }
  ],
  "keys": [],
  "functions": []
}
